  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 125 AM CDT Sun Jul 5 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will push the stalled front back northeast, and \ndry weather will return to our entire CWA for the rest of the work\nweek. Hot and dry weather will be the foreast each day. \nTemperatures will rise a few degrees by Friday, but heat indices \nwill remain below Heat Advisory levels for most of the CWA. A few \nspots in the east could reach advisory level each afternoon \nThursday through Saturday. Saturday another upper trough will ride\nover the ridge to the southeast US. This will bring another front\nnorth TX. This will bring a chance for showers and thunderstorms \nto South-Central Texas Saturday.",
